{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1557877-attribute-enhancing-quantum-powers-and-mega-edges","id":1557877,"title":"Attribute-enhancing quantum powers and mega edges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-24T11:02:57-08:00","id":1557877,"title":"Attribute-enhancing quantum powers and mega edges","content":"So, we have a couple different quantum powers capable of adding temporary mega attributes, like Boost, Growth and Transform. However, how does this work with mega-edges linked to those powers? I imagine the power of those edges gets boosted accordingly, but are there any ways to actually gain said mega edges from the powers? Or do you just need to already get the required minimum level of mega-attributes and then get the mega-edge?<br /> <br /> I guess that might make sense, balancing-wise, it might be a tad broken to be able to use Transform to get not only mega-dexterity 3 but also mega-speed, defense and accuracy. But it does feel sort of weird in certain cases. For instance, if you use Transform to turn into a jaguar, it would be sort of weird you already need to have mega-dexterity 1 and mega-speed in order to gain the speed of a jaguar from the transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-26T14:54:20-08:00","id":1557928,"title":"","content":"Maybe it has been a bit, but my read of Transform would allow you to pick up mega edges. I don't think Boost or Growth would, but I think that is a feature of Transform.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T22:21:55-08:00","id":1557959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1557877-attribute-enhancing-quantum-powers-and-mega-edges?p=1557928#post1557928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it has been a bit, but my read of Transform would allow you to pick up mega edges. I don't think Boost or Growth would, but I think that is a feature of Transform.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember Transform only allows you to pick sensory mega edges, Body Modification and Toughness. Which is interesting, since most sensory edges use mega-cunning as their base, while Transform can only give physical mega attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}